      "title": "In the laboratory",
      "place": "",
      "note": "Not photography exactly, but some of the most beautiful things I have seen were down a microscope, and some of the most satisfying were drawn by hand. A metal sphere surrounded by silicate melt — a core and a mantle, made by a master's student who could not speak for a minute afterwards. And the drawings: I like making diagrams almost as much as making experiments, and these, from the thesis, are how I explain a press, a sample assembly or a planet to someone who has never seen one.",
